  "resolution_html": "<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>Open <strong>Outlook</strong> and click <strong>New Email</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Go to the <strong>Options</strong> tab in the toolbar</li>\n</ol>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>Click <strong>Encrypt</strong> (lock icon)</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li>If you see “Connect to Rights Management Servers and Get templates”, select it and wait for Outlook to update</li>\n</ul>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2026/02/1-400x160.png\"/></figure>\n<ul>\n<li>Choose <strong>Encrypt</strong> to protect content. A banner will appear at the top of your email stating that the message is encrypted and recipients can’t remove it. Visit Microsoft’s support page to read more about the <a href=\"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/office/send-encrypted-messages-with-a-microsoft-365-personal-or-family-subscription-3521aa01-77e3-4cfd-8a13-299eb60b1957\">encryption options</a></li>\n</ul>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://www.yorku.ca/uit/infosec/wp-content/uploads/sites/806/2026/02/2-4-2026-9-58-04-AM-2-400x297.png\"/></figure>",
